"When an entity is feared (forced into the cowering stance), MOST actions become unavailable and are filtered out of the derived action set entirely — not shown. Model it with a stat requirement (an 'upright' gate, or better a 'steadiness' stat) that fear drives below the threshold most actions need, exactly like a prone stance's low gait starves the movement action. Rally requires no such steadiness, so it remains — and should be surfaced FRONT AND CENTER. Even Stand should snap the feared entity right back to cowering (changing stance doesn't escape fear; only Rally does). This also resolves the cowering game-feel trap (a player couldn't tell why they were stuck): with only Rally available, the state is self-evident."